    <DataNode elementId="AT5G14950-MONOMER" textLabel="Alpha-mannosidase 2" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q9LFR0" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="355" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">This golgi-localized a-mannosidase II (GMII) enzyme appears to be involved in the formation of complex N-glycans in Arabidopsis. A purified recombinant enzyme is able to catalyze the removal of &amp;alpha;1,3- and &amp;alpha;1,6-mannosyl residues from the &amp;alpha;1,6-mannose branch of N-glycans &lt;i&gt;in vitro&lt;/i&gt; and there is evidence from mutants lacking this enzyme that it performs the same function &lt;i&gt;in planta&lt;/i&gt; |CITS: [16460512]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT5G14950-MONOMER" />
